den","sight",-33.844,151.208,"Foreshore, Lavender Bay","","","","","r","Wendy Whitely, the widow of famed Australian landscape painter Brett Whiteley, has cleared out disused railway land in Lavender Bay to create a large, unofficial park, packed dense with Australian and exotic flowers."],["North Sydney Olympic Pool","activity",-33.84957,151.21172,"","Closed until 2026 due to renovations (likely longer due to budget blowouts)","","","","r","An outdoor public pool almost under the Harbour Bridge with spectacular views. It opened in 1936 and features sea water, sauna and outside snack area. Conveniently close to Sydney CBD. Winter water temperature can be very cold."],["Bridge Climb","activity",-33.85806,151.20694,"","","","","","r","You can climb to the top of the arch of the bridge. For those who are good with heights and enjoy a spectacular view of the harbour, there are organised climbs to the top of the bridge. This climb is more demanding than climbing a set…"],["Garrison Church","sight",-33.8584,151.206,"60 Lower Fort St","","","","","r","The colony's first military church, it is still an active Anglican church."],["Marrinawi Cove","activity",-33.85556,151.20192,"Barangaroo Point Reserve, Barangaroo","","","","","r","Free swimming spot in the harbour! Shark netting installed. Free showers as well, but no other facilities. Cafes are close by, however."],["The Wharf Theatre","activity",-33.85514,151.20353,"4/5 Hickson Rd","","","","","r","Pier Walsh Bay, on an old, renovated finger wharf. There is a bar and restaurant open during the show and at intermission. Booking for the restaurant is a good idea."]]}